  "practice": [
    "Say the name অনুস্বার (onushshar / anusvara), then practice ং as an ng-like nasal sound.",
    "Read রং, বাংলা, সংগীত, and ভয়ংকর aloud and listen for their nasal quality.",
    "Compare the small sign ং with the full consonant ঙ in রং/রঙিন and বাংলা/বাঙালি.",
    "Notice how ং blends with the following consonant in সংবাদ, সংগীত, and সংস্কৃতি."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ং is called অনুস্বার (onushshar / anusvara). It is a nasal sign, not a vowel.",
    "For beginners, ং ≈ ng is a useful reading shortcut, as in রং (rong), বাংলা (Bangla), and ভয়ংকর (bhoyongkor).",
    "The exact nasal pronunciation can shift with the following consonant: সংবাদ is shongbad, সংগীত is shonggit, and সংস্কৃতি is shongskriti.",
    "Do not confuse ং, the small anusvara sign, with ঙ, a full consonant. বাংলা and রং contain ং, while বাঙালি and রঙিন contain ঙ."
  ]
